  "created": "2022-03-17T00:11:49.207Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "EDIT:\n\nI figured out with help of some of the folks in the vrc discord.\nApparently the collider generation in avatar dynamics doesn't like it if your finger bones aren't all roughly the same length. So with some small adjustments to the armature, this was resolved.\n\nOriginal post is below\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nChanging the finger collider \"height\" (length) adjustment on the descriptor doesn't have any effect in game if the value is smaller than what it was on \"Automatic\". If you take a look at the images, you can see the way it shows in the editor, vs in game. \n\nIf the \"height\" is set to a value greater than or equal to than what was set in automatic mode, then it works fine. \nHowever if the \"height\" is set to a value smaller than the original, it appears to work fine in the editor, but just shows as the original length when in-game.\n\nThis is really annoying because the \"Automatic\" for some reason always decides to give a length value that is way too long. And because of this bug, I cannot manually fix it.",
